Content:  **Goal** – Starting from the two low‑scoring docked “lead” molecules, locate natural‑product‑like analogues that (i) keep a good (negative) docking score against the *Methyl‑Coenzyme‑M reductase* (MCR) binding site, (ii) interact with **at least two** of the required residues (F43602, PHE360, PHE440, TYR366, UNK0), (iii) have acceptable drug‑like/rumen‑compatible physicochemical properties, (iv) are synthetically accessible (low SAS) and (v) are commercially obtainable.

Below is the step‑by‑step screening that was performed with the available tools.

---

